WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:02.926
- Good morning Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael

00:00:02.926 --> 00:00:05.035
and my one word is "Believe" and I believe

00:00:05.035 --> 00:00:07.933
that entrepreneurs are going
to solve all of the world's

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:09.343
major problems.

00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:11.626
So to help you on your journey
today, we're going to learn

00:00:11.626 --> 00:00:14.262
how to have fun.

00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:16.032
Over to you, Hugh Jackman.

00:00:16.032 --> 00:00:18.167
(rooster crowing)

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.750
(groovy music)

00:00:27.456 --> 00:00:30.024
- When the things most
matter, you so desperately

00:00:30.024 --> 00:00:32.529
don't want to destroy it for being scared

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:34.575
that you can really destroy it.

00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:37.658
When I hosted the Oscars, I was like

00:00:37.658 --> 00:00:39.969
"Wow man, this is a billion
people", and I just thought,

00:00:39.969 --> 00:00:42.717
"Okay, whatever you do
just remember you're

00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:45.947
"a kid form Moringa in Sydney,
you're hosting the Oscars,

00:00:45.947 --> 00:00:49.056
"have some fun", you
know and, luckily for me,

00:00:49.056 --> 00:00:52.986
those turning points, I've
somehow always stuck to that idea

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.399
of just having fun.

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:56.828
- If you're not having fun,
you're never going to shine.

00:00:56.828 --> 00:00:58.874
If you're not having fun and
you're constantly stressed

00:00:58.874 --> 00:01:01.017
and you're constantly
worried and you're constantly

00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:03.455
freaking out, then you're
not going to have fun,

00:01:03.455 --> 00:01:04.979
your customers aren't going to have fun,

00:01:04.979 --> 00:01:06.676
your suppliers aren't going to have fun,

00:01:06.676 --> 00:01:07.792
and you're never going to be
able to build the business

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:08.939
that you want to build.

00:01:08.939 --> 00:01:10.984
I think you have to attack
it from both sides where

00:01:10.984 --> 00:01:15.264
you want to build a better
future, you want to be upset

00:01:15.264 --> 00:01:17.181
about what you've created,
and you want to build

00:01:17.181 --> 00:01:18.197
something greater.

00:01:18.197 --> 00:01:21.203
And at the same time have
fun, and be grateful,

00:01:21.203 --> 00:01:23.481
and recognize all the
amazing things that you have

00:01:23.481 --> 00:01:24.561
currently built up.

00:01:24.561 --> 00:01:25.867
It's both.

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:29.059
If all you're doing is fun,
happy, la la la and you never

00:01:29.059 --> 00:01:31.591
strive to improve, and
if all you're focusing on

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:35.020
is improvement and getting
better then you're never happy.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.560
You need to have both.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.104
One of the things that I've
encouraged my instructors

00:01:38.104 --> 00:01:40.835
here to do at Toronto
Dance Salsa is to have fun

00:01:40.835 --> 00:01:42.389
in their class.

00:01:42.389 --> 00:01:44.759
And their students will have fun,

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:47.710
our customers will have
fun if the instructor

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.919
is genuinely having fun.

00:01:49.919 --> 00:01:52.653
And that looks different
for different people.

00:01:52.653 --> 00:01:55.083
One instructor might tell
a lot of silly jokes,

00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:57.555
one instructor might
be goofy at the front,

00:01:57.555 --> 00:01:59.988
one instructor might put on a song

00:01:59.988 --> 00:02:01.662
that makes him really happy.

00:02:01.662 --> 00:02:03.940
It doesn't matter what it
is, it has to be individual

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.947
to each person and I
can't tell that person

00:02:05.947 --> 00:02:07.867
"Here's what you need
to do to have more fun",

00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:09.464
they already know.

00:02:09.464 --> 00:02:12.644
But for their class to be more fun,

00:02:12.644 --> 00:02:16.787
they have to actually be
having fun in the class.

00:02:16.787 --> 00:02:19.646
And so if you take that to your business,

00:02:19.646 --> 00:02:22.582
yes you want to strive,
yes you want to grow,

00:02:22.582 --> 00:02:24.927
yes you want to push,
yes you want the best,

00:02:24.927 --> 00:02:28.658
yes you want to improve,
and, at the same time,

00:02:28.658 --> 00:02:31.802
you want to enjoy what you
have, you want to have fun,

00:02:31.802 --> 00:02:34.272
you want to be grateful,
and you want to remember

00:02:34.272 --> 00:02:36.710
this moment as something
special in history.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.905
Sometimes it can be hard
to remember to do it

00:02:38.905 --> 00:02:41.902
but even just a simple reminder can help.

00:02:41.902 --> 00:02:44.815
If you feel yourself
getting really stressed out,

00:02:44.815 --> 00:02:48.709
freaking out, not being
clear, snapping at people,

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:51.292
just a reminder to say,

00:02:52.661 --> 00:02:54.722
"How can I have a little
more fun in this?"

00:02:54.722 --> 00:02:56.766
or, "What am I grateful for today?" Or,

00:02:56.766 --> 00:02:58.745
"How can I make this situation better?"

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:01.678
to cool yourself down, gain
a little more perspective,

00:03:01.678 --> 00:03:04.035
and help you go off and
accomplish the big goals

00:03:04.035 --> 00:03:05.341
that you've set for yourself.

00:03:05.341 --> 00:03:09.039
So the question today is,
I'm curious what do you do

00:03:09.039 --> 00:03:12.968
in your business to have a little fun?

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.223
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:03:14.223 --> 00:03:15.461
super curious to find out.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.657
I also want to give a
quick shoutout to Shoaib,

00:03:17.657 --> 00:03:21.095
I hope I pronounced that
okay, from hmshost.com.

00:03:21.095 --> 00:03:23.038
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:03:23.038 --> 00:03:25.105
"Your One Word", I really appreciate it

00:03:25.105 --> 00:03:27.026
and I hope you're enjoying reading it.

00:03:27.026 --> 00:03:29.701
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.671
Ii hope you continue
to believe in yourself

00:03:31.671 --> 00:03:33.781
and whatever your one word is.

00:03:33.781 --> 00:03:36.327
Much love and I will see
you again tomorrow morning

00:03:36.327 --> 00:03:39.620
for another shot of entspresso.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.203
(groovy music)

00:03:47.813 --> 00:03:49.452
- [Reporter] So something like
Avengers, it seems like you

00:03:49.452 --> 00:03:51.045
were having a great time.
- I am.

00:03:51.045 --> 00:03:53.343
- [Reporter] Not a huge
acting challenge for you,

00:03:53.343 --> 00:03:55.324
I'd imagine, but-
- That depends.

00:03:55.324 --> 00:03:56.860
[Reporter] You seem to be having fun.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.316
- Well fun is important,
this should be a fun job.

00:03:59.316 --> 00:04:00.508
It's make believe.

00:04:00.508 --> 00:04:03.540
It's you and your friends
with real costumes

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:07.590
and better guns and
(muted) doing the thing,

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:08.915
exciting people.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.379
That's what that's about.

00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:12.348
When you're doing something
like The Avengers,

00:04:12.348 --> 00:04:15.733
you got to take it seriously in terms of

00:04:15.733 --> 00:04:18.876
you believe the space you're
in, you believe the world

00:04:18.876 --> 00:04:21.593
and the convention of it, that
there are people who can do

00:04:21.593 --> 00:04:24.181
(muted) greater than
normal human beings can do.

00:04:24.181 --> 00:04:27.419
Trust that, go with it,
treat them like they're those

00:04:27.419 --> 00:04:29.893
kinds of people and they
have an element of danger

00:04:29.893 --> 00:04:33.690
and an element of awe
that comes with all that.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.554
That's the honesty of the world.

00:04:35.554 --> 00:04:39.531
But I'm (muted) Nick Fury, I
got some (muted) with me, too.

00:04:39.531 --> 00:04:41.727
So I can be, you know, boom.

00:04:41.727 --> 00:04:44.368
I can stand up to them
and say what I need to say

00:04:44.368 --> 00:04:47.159
and sometimes, like in The
Avengers, I need to manipulate

00:04:47.159 --> 00:04:50.100
these people, I got to
where I an because I'm

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.253
Nick (muted) Fury, I can do some (muted).

00:04:52.253 --> 00:04:55.156
Nobody know how old I am
or why I'm still alive.

00:04:55.156 --> 00:04:58.222
Or why I'm now black
when I used to be white.

00:04:58.222 --> 00:04:59.867
So I got some (muted) with me too.

00:04:59.867 --> 00:05:03.457
So you could accept that and
you go with it and you treat it

00:05:03.457 --> 00:05:05.316
like it's something
honest and you treat it

00:05:05.316 --> 00:05:07.723
like it's something real so
when people come and see it,

00:05:07.723 --> 00:05:09.395
they don't see you going

00:05:09.395 --> 00:05:10.878
(snorts)

00:05:10.878 --> 00:05:12.459
you know, I'm in it.

00:05:12.459 --> 00:05:14.311
I'm in it, its some
dangerous (muted) happening

00:05:14.311 --> 00:05:16.724
and you (muted) can help us fix that.

00:05:16.724 --> 00:05:19.448
So lets go get 'em, you
and your friends doing

00:05:19.448 --> 00:05:20.696
that (muted) when you're kids.

00:05:20.696 --> 00:05:22.995
"Lets go get 'em, lets go get 'em".

00:05:22.995 --> 00:05:25.341
And then you shoot a (muted)
and they can't say you missed.

00:05:25.341 --> 00:05:27.132
Cause the chest blow up and all that kind

00:05:27.132 --> 00:05:28.490
of (muted) happens, it's great.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:31.003
- So even with these
movies under your belt,

00:05:31.003 --> 00:05:33.380
you came out to L.A. and
you're still thinking

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.136
it was going to be for P.A. work.

00:05:35.136 --> 00:05:38.434
- I still thought it was
going to be P.A. work.

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:41.357
I mean I didn't know, still...

00:05:41.357 --> 00:05:43.787
I was believing more, I
mean, I shouldn't like

00:05:43.787 --> 00:05:45.251
that I was doing it and I had people,

00:05:45.251 --> 00:05:48.134
and I couldn't, honestly at that time,

00:05:48.134 --> 00:05:51.245
the 328 hours I was like,

00:05:51.245 --> 00:05:52.740
"Is this legal?"

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.967
Cause it was so much fun and I was

00:05:54.967 --> 00:05:56.756
(laughter)

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.667
I was really looking over
my shoulder going "Hmm".

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:01.351
(laughter)

00:06:01.351 --> 00:06:03.039
And I kept getting invited back.

00:06:03.039 --> 00:06:04.477
And then I had people coming up going,

00:06:04.477 --> 00:06:06.083
"Hey man, you're good
at this" and I was like,

00:06:06.083 --> 00:06:09.131
"Well thanks cause it sure is fun".

00:06:09.131 --> 00:06:11.131
So I really didn't know,

00:06:12.803 --> 00:06:15.601
I guess secretly, if I look
back and I look at my diaries,

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.803
there was hope underlined
but I was still like

00:06:17.803 --> 00:06:20.777
I needed to go out and get
a job and if I could pursue

00:06:20.777 --> 00:06:22.274
acting on the side.

00:06:22.274 --> 00:06:26.262
Get a P.A. job, get the story
telling biz behind the camera

00:06:26.262 --> 00:06:27.429
and let's see.

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:33.968
Then another funny thing happened.

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:36.097
That first audition when I got out here

00:06:36.097 --> 00:06:39.205
was for a caster called Hank McCahn.

00:06:39.205 --> 00:06:40.610
Know who I'm talking about?

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.191
It was for a film called
"Boys in the Side".

00:06:43.191 --> 00:06:45.904
And I went and read and he
goes, "You did really good,

00:06:45.904 --> 00:06:50.003
"I'll have you for a call
back sometime later".

00:06:50.003 --> 00:06:54.759
I went off from there, I get called in

00:06:54.759 --> 00:06:58.910
for a baseball film,
"Angels in the Outfield".

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:00.760
I walk in the door.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.382
There's a bunch of funny peculiarities.

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:06.605
How the hell I got to standing here today?

00:07:06.605 --> 00:07:09.750
I walk in the door to this
back lid, I remember I had

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:12.273
an American cap on, it was
on Warner Brother's lab,

00:07:12.273 --> 00:07:14.564
I open up the door, it was
back lit in the afternoon,

00:07:14.564 --> 00:07:16.548
the producer is sitting on the
couch, he looks up and goes,

00:07:16.548 --> 00:07:19.715
"Hey it's Jimmy, the All-American kid.

00:07:20.989 --> 00:07:23.547
"You ever play baseball?"
I said "12 years", he says,

00:07:23.547 --> 00:07:25.577
"You got the job".

00:07:25.577 --> 00:07:29.177
(laughter and applause)

00:07:29.177 --> 00:07:34.044
So they said to me they're
paying me Schedule-F, 48.5.

00:07:34.044 --> 00:07:37.010
$48,500 to go play baseball
for eleven weeks in Oakland,

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:40.162
again I'm going "What is this business?".

00:07:40.162 --> 00:07:42.616
But it happened and during
that I got called back

00:07:42.616 --> 00:07:44.183
to read for Herbert
Ross' "Boys on the Side"

00:07:44.183 --> 00:07:47.399
and got that role so
that Cohen Brother's film

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:50.435
that got pushed, that P.A.
job that I would've taken

00:07:50.435 --> 00:07:53.786
if it was there and it never happened.

00:07:53.786 --> 00:07:55.513
I have a P.A. stand.

00:07:55.513 --> 00:07:57.763
(laughter)

00:07:58.955 --> 00:08:01.455
(disco music)

00:08:13.623 --> 00:08:15.995
- By the way, I believe
in winners and losers

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.166
and especially the freedom to fail.

00:08:18.166 --> 00:08:22.032
- (both) Who him? Me? Who?

00:08:22.032 --> 00:08:24.532
(disco music)

00:08:30.208 --> 00:08:31.041
- No way!

00:08:36.278 --> 00:08:37.195
- Have fun!

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:40.393
You're not going to have fun
every minute of every day,

00:08:40.393 --> 00:08:43.318
I'd dont care what job you take, you know.

00:08:43.318 --> 00:08:46.966
Any job you take, I don't care
how well rewarded you are,

00:08:46.966 --> 00:08:51.115
I don't care anything about
that, it won't happen all

00:08:51.115 --> 00:08:55.282
the time but you better be
having fun in what you do.

00:08:56.844 --> 00:09:00.678
The truth is a lot of success
won't just come from ideas

00:09:00.678 --> 00:09:04.697
and being hardcore and
being in the weight room.

00:09:04.697 --> 00:09:07.914
A lot of your success is
going to come from luck.

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:11.326
I know that was true in my
case and I know, frankly,

00:09:11.326 --> 00:09:14.915
it's the case of almost
every successful entrepreneur

00:09:14.915 --> 00:09:19.060
I met in the tech business
in the last 34 years.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:22.666
People will make it seem like
it was the grandmaster plan

00:09:22.666 --> 00:09:26.833
and all cases of an all knowing
and an all seeing genius,

00:09:28.114 --> 00:09:32.281
that and a lot of luck is
what really leads to success.

00:09:33.271 --> 00:09:35.819
So given that you're going
to have to have a lot luck,

00:09:35.819 --> 00:09:38.229
you better be having a lot of fun.

00:09:38.229 --> 00:09:41.776
Don't take the next job or
don't do the next start-up

00:09:41.776 --> 00:09:45.245
because you "should", do
it because you want to.

00:09:45.245 --> 00:09:48.711
Because you can think of
nothing better, more exciting,

00:09:48.711 --> 00:09:52.336
more energizing to get
up every day and go do

00:09:52.336 --> 00:09:55.419
the whatever it is that you selected.

00:09:58.174 --> 00:10:02.920
Be patient when you get the
first signs that it's not fun

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:05.599
because time must be measured.

00:10:05.599 --> 00:10:09.077
Constantly be improving yourself.

00:10:09.077 --> 00:10:11.445
Cause only by improving
yourself will you maybe

00:10:11.445 --> 00:10:13.112
find that next idea.

00:10:14.253 --> 00:10:16.156
I'm sure there are many
people in this audience

00:10:16.156 --> 00:10:18.103
who'd like to do a start up.

00:10:18.103 --> 00:10:20.826
And yet, first of all to do a start up,

00:10:20.826 --> 00:10:22.719
is you got to have an idea.

00:10:22.719 --> 00:10:25.476
But if you're having fun, if
you're building capabilities,

00:10:25.476 --> 00:10:28.095
if you're treasuring your
time, if you're building

00:10:28.095 --> 00:10:30.268
your muscle and being hardcore,

00:10:30.268 --> 00:10:32.935
the good ideas will come to you.

